{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses","id":969625,"title":"How flexible/dramatic are Nimbuses?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-14T20:26:58-07:00","id":969625,"title":"How flexible/dramatic are Nimbuses?","content":"Nimbi? I'm not good with fancy plurals. Anyway, are there limits to how you can narrate a Nimbus manifesting? Could it appear as a ghostly figure that steps forward and casts the spell? Could it appear as a phantasmal creature representing the spell? Could it cause armor or weapons to appear on the Mage as a representation of the spell's effect? As a very specific example, could I narrate that an Obrimos forces spell issues forth from an array of shimmering golden cannons that fire with the sounds of trumpets, instead of just happening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T17:20:39-07:00","id":970327,"title":"","content":"It is my understanding that a Nimbus represents the Mage, not the spell cast so it probably wouldn't change much to reflect spells in effect. Other than that I think the only limitation is that it is a local phenomenon centered on the Mage. There have been examples of visual manifestations like your armor and weapons, of sounds such as screaming or Gregorian Chant, smells such as brimstone or honeysuckle, all meant to reflect the nature of the Mage himself.<br /> To me it sounds like second edition actually asks for two variations on your nimbus, one with a positive effect and one threatening and negative. Still not sure about that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6084,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","user":"2ptTakrill","date":". 09-15-2016, 08:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T19:19:05-07:00","id":970403,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a Nimbus isn't an effect of the spell being cast, its an effect that always accompanies your mage and flares depending on what you're doing. There are basically three types of Nimbus associated with your characters. A Long-term Nimbus, an Immediate Nimbus and a Signature Nimbus.<br /> <br /> The Long-term Nimbus is an effect associated with your characters Path that is always on and warping the world around them to a minor extent (until higher Gnosis, but that's later). This can be minor things like a Thrysus having the potency of alcohol in his immediate area becoming more potent or an Obrimos causing more than normal static electricity to build up in his immediate surrounds. <br /> <br /> The Immediate Nimbus is the one most people think about and is the most obvious and flashy. This is the mage being bathed in holy light as they fire off their spells, or shadows leaping and capering across the wall behind the mage. Of note though, these are normally only able to be perceived with mage sight. They also cause tilts which are related to the nature of the nimbus and have to be designed by both you and the ST for your game.<br /> <br /> Finally, the Signature Nimbus is probably the most subtle and only comes up when someone is scrutinizing an area where spells were cast previously (and your Immediate Nimbus flared). Its a, unique to you, magical fingerprint you leave behind after casting. With the aforementioned Thrysus and his alcohol potency, it might be a strong smell of honeyed mead or with a foul Sceletus it might be a tactile sensation of a slimy slick of oil coating the hand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T21:52:57-07:00","id":970482,"title":"","content":"Ah. That's a bit disheartening. I really wish it was more flavorful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:30:42-07:00","id":970501,"title":"","content":"It can be just as flavorful as you imagine, certainly most of your requested examples could be part of an Immediate Nimbus, and well not normally effected by whatever spell you cast it would certainly reflect your path. Don't forget it's your game, if you want the Nimbus to reflect your spells and everyone at the table agrees then house rule it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-15T22:38:03-07:00","id":970504,"title":"","content":"It's just a general problem I've had with Mage, is that the magic just doesn't really feel flavorful or fun. It's just &quot;think and something happens&quot;. It's definitely not like how magic shows up in horror fiction. <br /> <br /> It's the same reason why people objected to not being able to shapeshifting in Beast, though Beast is actually a counterexample; because I've always visualized Atavisms as working by manifesting a phantasmal image of part of your horror, which is pretty cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:03:20-07:00","id":970541,"title":"","content":"I'll admit the reason I was never that interested in Mage: the Ascension was because the spheres didn't feel like 'magic' with a 'c' to me, cool as the paradigm theory is. Personally I'm hoping Signs of Sorcery will help add a 'wizard' feel to the game. I really like the idea of Reach and Yantras for that reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T00:36:56-07:00","id":970553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=970504#post970504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's just a general problem I've had with Mage, is that the magic just doesn't really feel flavorful or fun.</div> </div> </div> </div>You clearly did not used Yantra system then...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T02:55:23-07:00","id":970596,"title":"","content":"----Expert from a recent session-----<br /> Lorraine: A young Law Student that experienced some strong Hallucinations. She dreamed she was &quot;Lagertha&quot;<br /> &quot;Cumberbatch&quot;: A police officer that saved Lorraine from some men-in-black and took her in an issolated coffee shop to talk about magick. <br /> .....<br /> &quot;But... I don't know how. Do I say some magic words or something?&quot; -Lorraine, with tones between disappointment and disbelief in her voice.<br /> &quot;It would help but you don't actually need to. Just conjure what you want to do in your mind and will it into existence&quot; -Cumberbatch, a-matter-of-fact<br /> <br /> Lorraine had enough of this. She lost the morning\u2019s lecture because of some stupid nightmare, she lost the midday\u2019s lecture because weird men in black chased her in class and was about to loose the rest because a policeman nicknamed &quot;Cumberbatch&quot; was asking her to order coffee with her mind.<br /> <br /> &quot;This is so stupid...&quot; -Lorraine<br /> <br /> Without knowing why she even tries, Lorraine stands up, goes to the edge of the mezzanine and glares the barista below, <b>her mind set on possessing him.</b><br /> .....<br /> <b>The Mind Arcanum in her Soul hears her inner call, her chains in Pandemonium now broken. Her Fallen Self is connected with her Supernal Path as Ravens of Shadows form through inner daemons she didn\u2019t knew she had.</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Her nimbus is Ravens of Shadow (Ravens, Norwegian Shadowname) and Broken Chains (Independence, Liberation)</span><br /> <br /> <b>But the torrent of Ravens is too strong. A tear appears briefly in the link between her Soul and Pandemonium. The channel simply can\u2019t hold the intensity of the Supernal Symbolism she asked for. </b><br /> <br /> <b>In pain, her Soul reaches for something less profane to affect the Fallen World.</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\">Possession (Making Mind of Potency) &quot;I possess the barista&quot;<br /> +1R: for trying something with higher Arcana. She can't cast Possession so she casts (House Rule)<br /> <br /> Psychic Domination (Ruling Mind of Potency) \u201cI command the barista\u201d<br /> +1R: for complex task (see spell) &quot;Make Coffee and bring it to me&quot;<br /> +1R: To cast as 1 turn instead of 3 hours<br /> +1R: To cast at distance without need to touch or aim<br /> +1R: To increase duration to one scene<br /> Total Reach 3 -&gt; Paradox = 3dice -&gt; Storyteller rolls -&gt; 2 Paradox Success. That means the spell is about to go wrong. She can spends one mana mana to reduce Paradox Successes by one.</span><br /> <br /> <b>Terrified, she spends raw magic to stabilize the Imago, but the breach spreads way too fast and the torrent of ravens goes out of control. </b><b>Lagertha feels the Abyssal forces trying to alter her spell and decides to shield it with the only thing she has left, her soul.</b><br /> <br /> <b>The breach between her Soul and Pandemonium heals, leaving the horrors of the Non-Existence outside the mortal Realms. But not before scaring the novice caster\u2019s Soul.</b><br /> \u2026..<br /> Back in the coffee shop, drops of blood fall from Lorraine\u2019s nostrils and black veins appear on her right hand.<br /> \u2026..<br /> <b>Then the Imago suddenly returns to order. The crows know by now what they\u2019ve been called to do. They fly and shove their beaks into the barista\u2019s brain transmiting directly the Supernal will of Lagertha.</b><br /> \u2026..<br /> Lorraine watches in awe and pain as the equally surprised man is making another Macchiato without knowing why.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T03:02:11-07:00","id":970600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadowjim12</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=970596#post970596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Total Reach 3 -&gt; Paradox = 3dice -&gt; Storyteller rolls -&gt; 2 Paradox Success. That means the spell is about to go wrong. She can spends one mana mana to reduce Paradox Successes by one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mana expenditure reduces the Paradox Dice Pool, not Paradox successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T03:18:06-07:00","id":970606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=970600#post970600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mana expenditure reduces the Paradox Dice Pool, not Paradox successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Woops,... I stand corrected. Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, I just wanted to share the Imago/Nimbus description. For me they are interelated.<br /> <br /> On the same session, Lorraine/Lagertha (PC) used mage sight and saw one of her professors &quot;Chained and used as a puppet&quot; while he was under the influence of Psychic Domination. I think it is more evocative than say &quot;The spell is mind 2&quot; or &quot;Has traces of mind magic&quot;.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6169-shadowjim12","name":"Shadowjim12","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T04:11:08-07:00","id":970614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=970504#post970504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's the same reason why people objected to not being able to shapeshifting in Beast, though Beast is actually a counterexample; because I've always visualized Atavisms as working by manifesting a phantasmal image of part of your horror, which is pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's official not just your visualization by the way. It's just that only supernaturals can see the image.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T06:56:34-07:00","id":970658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses#post969625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nimbi? I'm not good with fancy plurals. Anyway, are there limits to how you can narrate a Nimbus manifesting? Could it appear as a ghostly figure that steps forward and casts the spell? Could it appear as a phantasmal creature representing the spell? Could it cause armor or weapons to appear on the Mage as a representation of the spell's effect? As a very specific example, could I narrate that an Obrimos forces spell issues forth from an array of shimmering golden cannons that fire with the sounds of trumpets, instead of just happening?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a question about your very specific example and the Obrimos using a Forces spell...<br /> <br /> Is this the Nimbus you want for your Obrimos? Or is this something specific to the spell; like, you are using the Forces magic to create a thunderous trumpeting sound or blast?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:05:57-07:00","id":970959,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=970658#post970658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have a question about your very specific example and the Obrimos using a Forces spell...<br /> <br /> Is this the Nimbus you want for your Obrimos? Or is this something specific to the spell; like, you are using the Forces magic to create a thunderous trumpeting sound or blast?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I'd prefer her Nimbus to manifest as gears and machine parts around her that make her seem as if she's wearing golden clockwork armor when she casts magic, since her Awakening heavily focused on deist concepts of divine machinery and crystal spheres. I want spells to manifest as tools or weapons appearing on the armor: a Forces attack summons a row of trumpet-shaped cannons that fire whatever it is the spell fires, telekinesis appears as spidery mechanical arms extending from the armor to manipulate objects, a flight spell would make wings or engines extend from the armor, and sensory spells cause a shining eyepiece to drop down from the helmet that she looks through.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:42:02-07:00","id":970976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=970959#post970959\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd prefer her Nimbus to manifest as gears and machine parts around her that make her seem as if she's wearing golden clockwork armor when she casts magic, since her Awakening heavily focused on deist concepts of divine machinery and crystal spheres. I want spells to manifest as tools or weapons appearing on the armor: a Forces attack summons a row of trumpet-shaped cannons that fire whatever it is the spell fires, telekinesis appears as spidery mechanical arms extending from the armor to manipulate objects, a flight spell would make wings or engines extend from the armor, and sensory spells cause a shining eyepiece to drop down from the helmet that she looks through.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of that sounds extremely awesome and if I were your ST I would I have no problem letting that be how your magic manifests. Another thing I'd suggest for you to consider: If your spell is going to end up being Vulgar... meaning that it will draw paradox whether your have witnesses or not and stuff like that... it's going to be very blatant, like telekinesis or whatever... <i>You can make it look however you like. You have an unlimited visual effect budget.</i> There's no difference between telekinesis where stuff just moves on it's own, or clockwork spider appendages manipulate items, or gusts of winds move items, or a giant glowing green hand, or spirits/ghost move the object... It's your mage's style and Nimbus and signature magic. It's very cool.<br /> <br /> It would be cool if someone examining the traces of your magic recognizes it by the faint sounds of tick-tock-tick-tock and the scent of gear oil...<br /> <br /> I think your idea is acceptable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/346-troy","name":"Troy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:48:35-07:00","id":970979,"title":"","content":"So wow, umm I was going to ask if having the image tree bearing fruit of exceeding white appear behind my mage is a good Nimbus for my Obrimos.<br /> <br /> The tree is a symbol in a vision from the prophet Lehi and a representation of God's Love.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T16:52:38-07:00","id":970982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Troy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=970976#post970976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> All of that sounds extremely awesome and if I were your ST I would I have no problem letting that be how your magic manifests. Another thing I'd suggest for you to consider: If your spell is going to end up being Vulgar... meaning that it will draw paradox whether your have witnesses or not and stuff like that... it's going to be very blatant, like telekinesis or whatever... <i>You can make it look however you like. You have an unlimited visual effect budget.</i> There's no difference between telekinesis where stuff just moves on it's own, or clockwork spider appendages manipulate items, or gusts of winds move items, or a giant glowing green hand, or spirits/ghost move the object... It's your mage's style and Nimbus and signature magic. It's very cool.<br /> <br /> It would be cool if someone examining the traces of your magic recognizes it by the faint sounds of tick-tock-tick-tock and the scent of gear oil...<br /> <br /> I think your idea is acceptable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! That was very helpful, and I'm glad you like my idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T17:00:28-07:00","id":970986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=970979#post970979\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So wow, umm I was going to ask if having the image tree bearing fruit of exceeding white appear behind my mage is a good Nimbus for my Obrimos.<br /> <br /> The tree is a symbol in a vision from the prophet Lehi and a representation of God's Love.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bIt's actually very similar to angel wings, pillars of light or dancing shadows. The Obrimos sense of having been called by a higher, divine, purpose also fits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T20:02:09-07:00","id":971104,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=970986#post970986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bIt's actually very similar to angel wings, pillars of light or dancing shadows. The Obrimos sense of having been called by a higher, divine, purpose also fits.</div> </div> </div> </div>And Nimbus Tilt? Is that chosen in advance or is it unique to the moment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T07:49:14-07:00","id":971314,"title":"","content":"I believe the Tilt is chosen when first designing the Nimbus.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:05:30-07:00","id":971324,"title":"","content":"You can &quot;completely rework&quot; the Nimbus Tilt every time you raise Gnosis. Otherwise it stays the same.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:18:12-07:00","id":971353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>2ptTakrill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971314#post971314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe the Tilt is chosen when first designing the Nimbus.</div> </div> </div> </div>Any good ideas for what would be fitting for my character?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 09-17-2016, 12:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:03:47-07:00","id":971412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971353#post971353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any good ideas for what would be fitting for my character?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The TIlt is chosen, but you can rework every time you gain a point of Gnosis. Edit: Ooh, Maina beat me to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8573-zombiecakes","name":"Zombiecakes","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"213"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:31:55-07:00","id":971463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Zombiecakes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971412#post971412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The TIlt is chosen, but you can rework every time you gain a point of Gnosis. Edit: Ooh, Maina beat me to it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still I'm not sure what to choose, a feeling of deep fatherly (love? Disappointment? Reproach?) that...has some sort of mechanical effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:59:34-07:00","id":971478,"title":"","content":"A tilt for a Nimbus that causes a feeling of fatherly love might grant a bonus to Composure if it makes you feel protected by a higher power. It might grant Resolve if it inspires you to do greater deeds for said power. Maybe both. Remember that the Tilt can give bonus or malus or even both, depending on what fits the fluff. People can choose not to resist a Tilt, after all, but your enemies have no reason to avoid resisting if they don't know your Tilt is beneficial.<br /> <br /> There can also be skill malus/bonus. My character's tilt gives a pacifying aura of peace and gives a malus to weaponry/brawl/firearms, for example. She has Potent Nimbus, so she managed to spread the penalty over three skills.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T16:19:59-07:00","id":971564,"title":"","content":"Hm, would it be possible to work it so that the Nimbus conceals the character's identity when active? Like, it acts as a representation of their Shadow Name/Persona and causes a mask to appear on them, or would that need to be houseruled?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T17:34:27-07:00","id":971599,"title":"","content":"A nimbus could appear as things like a mask, however, a nimbus is unique to your character and after flaring leaves the signature nimbus. So while it may obscure your features, it actually marks out who you are to other mages who know/know of you. Also don't forget that typically, Sleeper witnesses can't even see the nimbus, so would just see you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:11:40-07:00","id":971624,"title":"","content":"Worth noting two things:<br /> <br /> 1. Sleeper witnesses do see the Nimbus if you deliberately flare it by spending mana, but they'll rationalize it away like all Supernal magic.<br /> <br /> 2. The Nimbus only lasts for a few seconds at most, so it's not very useful as a disguise even if it did mask your identity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T18:47:39-07:00","id":971649,"title":"","content":"Ah. Would it be possible to hack it to make it last longer? That would be better for the armor idea I mentioned before.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T19:25:12-07:00","id":971671,"title":"","content":"The Nimbus is always there, if a Mage looks at you with Focused Mage Sight he'll see it. If you want to make the visual effect last longer, use Prime. The Nimbus is under its purview.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:15:29-07:00","id":971708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971671#post971671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nimbus is always there, if a Mage looks at you with Focused Mage Sight he'll see it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s wholly invisible except when spellcasting, and even then only to Mage Sight most of the time. </div> </div> </div>Page 88. The Immediate Nimbus is only visible when Spellcasting. Focused Mage Sight does not reveal it. Unless something hidden away in a corner of the book contradicts the Nimbus and Mage Sight sections, which would not surprise me. Focused Mage Sight can study the Signature Nimbus, but it is not always present. It is only present for about a week (longer with high Gnosis) after you cast spells on things, and it's only visible on that thing. Long-Term Nimbus is never really visible as near as I can tell.<br /> <br /> Prime does cover the Nimbus though, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T20:45:14-07:00","id":971725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971353#post971353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Any good ideas for what would be fitting for my character?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGiven the Tree of Life image either a bonus to Composure or Resolve would fit as all present feel connected to a divine power. I could also see a bonus on Empathy checks involving interaction or on Persuasion as the Mage gives off a sense of benevolence, perhaps even outright eliminating a door as the Mage is pushed further up the friendship ladder. It might be reasonable to claim it interferes with gaining Willpower points from fulfilling Vice. For a really dramatic effect it might be fun if it dims the rage of Werewolves and Wrath spirits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T22:12:29-07:00","id":971769,"title":"","content":"I'll save that last one for after I gained some Gnosis but bonus to Empathy sounds about right. I'll start there I think and then move up to draining away rage. Though maybe I'll have it start with influence over rage, just need to figure out the mechanics oft of the situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T23:15:20-07:00","id":971787,"title":"","content":"I'm mostly trying to work the Nimbus to be more dramatic because I'm trying to like Mage and part of that is finding a way to make spellcasting interesting and flavorful. My current problem is that there are no character concepts I have for Mage that I wouldn't enjoy more elsewhere. I still haven't come up with a reason why, say, I'd want to make an Obrimos instead of a Demon or a God-Machine cultist.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T04:02:07-07:00","id":971863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971787#post971787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mostly trying to work the Nimbus to be more dramatic because I'm trying to like Mage and part of that is finding a way to make spellcasting interesting and flavorful. My current problem is that there are no character concepts I have for Mage that I wouldn't enjoy more elsewhere. I still haven't come up with a reason why, say, I'd want to make an Obrimos instead of a Demon or a God-Machine cultist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your right in that a Machine Cultist and a Obrimos can both summon angelic beings, the Seraph and Cherubim that the Orbrimos summons though have nothing to do with the God Machine they are natives of Aether. They are Supernal beings, and my character Ammon is an Obrimos. I could never see him as a God Machine Cultist. Ammon questions the role of magic and it's relationship to divinity, he questions if using magic its self is damning to the soul or uplifting. He in his heart questions the rest of what the Pentacle says is true because to him, and his mind he has to ask if it is true? What about the things he knew to be true in his past how do those relate?<br /> <br /> A God machine cultist doesn't question, a Mage does, constantly. And once they find an answer, they've found the next question.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T04:17:28-07:00","id":971870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971863#post971863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Your right in that a Machine Cultist and a Obrimos can both summon angelic beings, the Seraph and Cherubim that the Orbrimos summons though have nothing to do with the God Machine they are natives of Aether. They are Supernal beings, and my character Ammon is an Obrimos. I could never see him as a God Machine Cultist. Ammon questions the role of magic and it's relationship to divinity, he questions if using magic its self is damning to the soul or uplifting. He in his heart questions the rest of what the Pentacle says is true because to him, and his mind he has to ask if it is true? What about the things he knew to be true in his past how do those relate?<br /> <br /> A God machine cultist doesn't question, a Mage does, constantly. And once they find an answer, they've found the next question.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's no reason why a God-Machine cultist or Stigmatic couldn't question and keep questioning, though. I know their powers come from different sources, that's not really relevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T04:31:53-07:00","id":971877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971870#post971870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's no reason why a God-Machine cultist or Stigmatic couldn't question and keep questioning, though. I know their powers come from different sources, that's not really relevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>A God-Machine cultist can't question and keep his powers though. His powers are based on his faith in the Machine. If he loses that faith or if it wavers for even a second, or has the slightest fluctuation he loses power, maybe not all of it but quite a bit of it.<br /> <br /> An Obrimos can question and keep his power, his faith can wane, wonder, he can allow himself to fall from his faith he can modify it, because it isn't his source of power it's how he first perceived the world of magic. Ammon can question if magic truly was a gift from Heavenly Father, or if it is a power that man is not meant to have yet who's origins lie elsewhere?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T07:37:33-07:00","id":971922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971787#post971787\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm mostly trying to work the Nimbus to be more dramatic because I'm trying to like Mage and part of that is finding a way to make spellcasting interesting and flavorful. My current problem is that there are no character concepts I have for Mage that I wouldn't enjoy more elsewhere. I still haven't come up with a reason why, say, I'd want to make an Obrimos instead of a Demon or a God-Machine cultist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me be frank with you. I don't think what you're doing is actually trying to like Mage. What you're doing is trying to turn Mage <i>into</i> something you like. There's a pretty big difference there. You don't <i>need</i> to like Mage, it doesn't <i>have</i> to be your cup of tea. If you would enjoy playing the character concepts you like elsewhere, don't try to force it into the confines of Mage, just go enjoy it using the mediums you would enjoy them best at.<br /> <br /> Hell, I don't like D&amp;D 3.5, and that seems to be one of the most widely popular pen and paper RPGs out there. I've tried to like it, but the mechanics just irritate me too much. Sure, I could try to Frankenstein the system into something completely different and maybe be halfway content with the results, but at the end of the day I save a lot of time, and frustration and then simply enjoy myself more by moving on to a different system that fits my preferences better. <br /> <br /> Now I'm not saying don't makes a few tweaks here and there to fix the occasional little thing you don't like, but if the game as a whole just isn't a fit for you it's usually better to just accept that it isn't your thing and proceed to enjoy the things that are.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2309-ashenrogue","name":"Ashenrogue","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1388"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T08:48:45-07:00","id":971947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971877#post971877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A God-Machine cultist can't question and keep his powers though. His powers are based on his faith in the Machine. If he loses that faith or if it wavers for even a second, or has the slightest fluctuation he loses power, maybe not all of it but quite a bit of it.<br /> <br /> An Obrimos can question and keep his power, his faith can wane, wonder, he can allow himself to fall from his faith he can modify it, because it isn't his source of power it's how he first perceived the world of magic. Ammon can question if magic truly was a gift from Heavenly Father, or if it is a power that man is not meant to have yet who's origins lie elsewhere?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. That's not how the Machine works. It isn't powered by faith or anything like that. Gaining power from the machine is equivalent to hacking reality. Stigmatics do not lose their powers if they lose faith in the Machine. <br /> <br /> The Machine does not care if you worship it or not. The Machine does not care what you think. The Machine simply Is. To suggest that you'd lose power derived from it if you didn't worship it is like saying that light bulbs only work if you worship electricity. I suggest you read Demon. The Machine is not a deity. The Machine Is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:17:43-07:00","id":971992,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971947#post971947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope. That's not how the Machine works. It isn't powered by faith or anything like that. Gaining power from the machine is equivalent to hacking reality. Stigmatics do not lose their powers if they lose faith in the Machine. <br /> <br /> The Machine does not care if you worship it or not. The Machine does not care what you think. The Machine simply Is. To suggest that you'd lose power derived from it if you didn't worship it is like saying that light bulbs only work if you worship electricity. I suggest you read Demon. The Machine is not a deity. The Machine Is.</div> </div> </div> </div>But it isn't about that, cultists get their powers by praying for them faith is key because without faith the prayer fails. Not because it displeased but because the cultists doesn't think it will work, and thus it will fail.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T10:44:04-07:00","id":972006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971992#post971992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But it isn't about that, cultists get their powers by praying for them faith is key because without faith the prayer fails. Not because it displeased but because the cultists doesn't think it will work, and thus it will fail.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't supported by any of the actual mechanics for cults. It's a nice thought, but Gecko is correct that that is not how any of it works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T17:43:09-07:00","id":972235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=971947#post971947\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gaining power from the machine is equivalent to hacking reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Machine does not care if you worship it or not. The Machine does not care what you think. </div> </div> </div>Which is why, if It's paying you any mind whatsoever, your powers will likely as not stop working the way you want them to just as soon as they've accomplished what It's let you have them to do.<br /> <br /> God-Machine cultists, shockingly, are cultists. There's a Persistent Condition that specifically makes you more susceptible to the God-Machine's influence by virtue of how overly trusting you are of an enormous otherworldly force.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T18:01:05-07:00","id":972244,"title":"","content":"The God-Machine Chronicle literally describes people hacking the machine. <br /> <br /> Stigmatics don't gain or lose power from belief. If that were the case, they couldn't be created by accident. <br /> <br /> These things don't need &quot;belief&quot; to work. This is not Ascension. A piece of malfunctioning Infrastructure that will generate guns that shoot teeth if the blood of a virgin goat is spilled on it will work regardless of whether or not the person doing it believes in magic. <br /> <br /> This is offtopic, just wanted to clear that up. To bring things back, I prefer those two options because, to me, being a machine-worshipping fanatic who manages to wrestle a very limited and incredibly dangerous amount of power from obsessive studies and plans is more suited to the setting then &quot;I blacked out and saw one of five things and now I shoot energy blasts.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T19:58:42-07:00","id":972297,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how insulting the core premise of the game line your topic is in really gets the discussion back on topic. I mean I could just as easily describe Mage as being a game about Atlantis worshipping fanatics who wrestle a very limited and incredibly dangerous amount of power from obsessive studies and plans, but if you really dislike the entirety of Mage, why are you trying to force a square peg into a round hole. If you like aspects of the ChroD mechanics, hack something together for your own table. Ranting about how bad Mage is, in the Mage section of the forums, just seems like you're looking to fight and argue with people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5439-gullinbursti","name":"Gullinbursti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5439_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"291"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:25:43-07:00","id":972304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Geckopirateship</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/969625-how-flexible-dramatic-are-nimbuses?p=972244#post972244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The God-Machine Chronicle literally describes people hacking the machine.<br /> <br /> Stigmatics don't gain or lose power from belief. If that were the case, they couldn't be created by accident.<br /> <br /> These things don't need &quot;belief&quot; to work. This is not Ascension. A piece of malfunctioning Infrastructure that will generate guns that shoot teeth if the blood of a virgin goat is spilled on it will work regardless of whether or not the person doing it believes in magic.<br /> <br /> This is offtopic, just wanted to clear that up. To bring things back, I prefer those two options because, to me, being a machine-worshipping fanatic who manages to wrestle a very limited and incredibly dangerous amount of power from obsessive studies and plans is more suited to the setting then &quot;I blacked out and saw one of five things and now I shoot energy blasts.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Stigmatics do not equal god machine cultists the first chapter fiction before the introduction of Demon clearly states that and proves it. Stigmatics seem more like the hackers, they accidentally stumbled upon something, were scared by it but in return got back door access.<br /> <br /> Cultists might have started off as Stigmatics but don't have to be. they can be people who were never scared by the machine who just worship it. They know the system codes and have admin access to some limited functions as long as it doesn't interfere with the plans of the machine or they are doing it's bidding. In whole though they get their power from the machine because it is granting it and it can take it away. I think I gave that trait to all cultists even human cultists of Papa wolf. Honestly it fits very fluffy wise and works wonderfully.<br /> <br /> Plus why worship the machine? Why not something else? Honestly the machine only needs to come up in Demon games, and in my other games well it only came up once in another as a McGuffin that was believed to be a machine created to make people into gods. It had deviated from it's original purpose but the series villains had managed to get the information and were in the process of becoming gods. So why be a cultist beholden to a machine god/the exarchs/some aliens/ made why not seek a path to true understanding? Why allow yourself to be chained down? though religion is common for Obromos it isn't for any other mages. A under taker fascinated by death and making the dead as lifelike as possible might just see though the illusions of death in this world and become a Moros. A master handyman, who uses techniques he learned from amish craftsmen who perfected the art of carpentry is also just as likely to become a moros. Neither of them have anything to do with religion.<br /> <br /> A police officer sworn to serve his fellow man, is also likely to become an orbrimos because justice and order become the obsessions that he uses to reach through the barrier of the lie and find the supernal. A Fire Fighter who risks his life going into burning buildings to pull people out, his courage and selflessness allow him to reach beyond the lie and emerge an Obrimos.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-18T20:42:17-07:00","id":972314,"title":"","content":"I don't know about wresting power from the God Machine, but if what you really want is the image/flavor of your Mage's magic resembling things like armor, cannon and mechanical limbs maybe what you should be looking at is the Shadow Persona merit. All of those things could be how your character views his/her magic and uses that image as a yantra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6084-2pttakrill","name":"2ptTakrill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"942"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-19T14:38:45-07:00","id":972733,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I'm sorry for going off on another rant, especially in the Mage section. This thread was really helpful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}